## Desired behavior
`PhysicsPrivate::CreateWorldEntities` in `src/systems/physics/Physics.cc` builds an `sdf::World` for `Engine::ConstructWorld` with the name and the gravity of the world only. The `<physics>` element of the world is not part of it, although the Physics system already uses it for its own options (collision detector, solver, max contacts).

A physics engine plugin that is not shipped with gz-physics cannot read its own settings from the SDF. We have a MuJoCo engine plugin for gz-physics that reads `<physics><gz:mujoco>...</gz:mujoco></physics>`, and it cannot get them through `ConstructWorld`.

The Physics system should put the `<physics>` profile of the world entity into the `sdf::World` it passes to `ConstructWorld`, so `sdf::World::PhysicsByIndex(0)->Element()` has the settings, including custom elements.

## Alternatives considered
* A parameter on `<plugin name="gz::sim::systems::Physics">` that the Physics system forwards to the engine: needs a new interface, while `sdf::World` already has a place for the physics profile.
* Reading the SDF file from the engine plugin: the engine does not know the file, and worlds can be generated or changed at runtime.

## Implementation suggestion
After `world.SetGravity(...)`:

```cpp
auto worldPhysics = _ecm.Component<components::Physics>(_entity);
if (worldPhysics)
{
  world.ClearPhysics();
  world.AddPhysics(worldPhysics->Data());
}
```

`SdfEntityCreator` creates `components::Physics` for every world (the default profile if the SDF has none), so an engine always gets one profile. Engines that ignore it are not affected.

## Additional context
Checked `main` (11.0.0-pre3): `ConstructWorld(world)` is still called with name and gravity only. I found no existing issue or PR for this.
